      "Language": "ita",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Fifty-five patients with osteoarthritis, rheumatoid arthritis or spondyloarthritis, joint pain and other rheumatic-inflammatory disorders were treated with proglumetacin, at different doses, during 3-60 days. Assessment of therapeutic efficacy indicated 88.9% of good results. Joint pain progressively decreased during the whole period of observation. Tolerance was considered good or very good in 78% of patients."},
